      "writtenOn": "2024-04-16T01:07:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is getting pretty complicated to convert errors and such. There are a few approaches I\u0027m thinking. Right now we have ServiceManagerShim. If you add another layer here, so it\u0027s ServiceManagerShim (thin layer) -in-process-\u003e AidlServiceManagerShim (thick layer which has the logic which is currently ServiceManagerShim) -in-process-\u003e theRealServiceManager.\n\nThen, you can use the binder API to convert AidlServiceManagerShim to IBinder, and the ServiceManagerNative code can use that directly. If this is done in a way that AidlServiceManagerShim preserves the errors from theRealServiceManager (and ServiceManagerShim collapses them), you could get most things for free (ignoring some of the C++/Java AIDL differences). WDYT?",
      "revId": "272e7a86558bb8fdc4d16523b4dc6daaa5162beb",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
